# Task: Fix VACE and MoCha Tab — Broken Upload and Disabled Generate Button

## 1. Context & Objective

Two bugs break the VACE and MoCha tabs in the Video Generator window:

**Bug 1 — File dialogs do nothing (affects VACE and MoCha):**
`FileDialogService.OpenFileDialogAsync` (and the other three dialog methods) call `Task.Run()` to execute `ShowDialog()` on a thread-pool thread. Thread-pool threads are MTA, but WPF file dialogs require an STA thread. The dialog throws `System.Threading.ThreadStateException` which propagates through the `async void` command handlers and is swallowed — so clicking Browse does nothing.

**Bug 2 — Mocha Generate button never enables:**
`VideoGeneratorViewModel.ForwardPropertyChanged` re-fires `PropertyChanged` from sub-ViewModels using the original property name. When `MochaVM.CanGenerateVideo` changes, it fires `PropertyChanged("CanGenerateVideo")` on the parent VM — but the Mocha Generate button's `IsEnabled` is bound to `CanGenerateMochaVideo`. The binding never receives a notification, so the button stays permanently disabled.

## 2. Files to Modify

- `FlipPix.UI/Services/FileDialogService.cs`
- `FlipPix.UI/ViewModels/VideoGeneratorViewModel.cs`

## 3. Implementation Steps

### Step 1 — Fix `FileDialogService.cs`

Add `using System.Windows;` at the top if not already present.

Replace all four dialog method bodies. Instead of `Task.Run(...)`, use `Application.Current.Dispatcher.InvokeAsync(...)` so the dialog runs on the WPF UI thread (which is STA).

**`OpenFileDialogAsync`** — replace body with:
```csharp
public Task<string?> OpenFileDialogAsync(string title, string filter, string? initialDirectory = null)
{
    return Application.Current.Dispatcher.InvokeAsync(() =>
    {
        var dialog = new Microsoft.Win32.OpenFileDialog
        {
            Title = title,
            Filter = filter,
            CheckFileExists = true,
            CheckPathExists = true
        };

        if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(initialDirectory) && System.IO.Directory.Exists(initialDirectory))
            dialog.InitialDirectory = initialDirectory;

        return dialog.ShowDialog() == true ? dialog.FileName : null;
    }).Task;
}
```

**`OpenFilesDialogAsync`** — replace body with:
```csharp
public Task<string[]> OpenFilesDialogAsync(string title, string filter, string? initialDirectory = null)
{
    return Application.Current.Dispatcher.InvokeAsync(() =>
    {
        var dialog = new Microsoft.Win32.OpenFileDialog
        {
            Title = title,
            Filter = filter,
            CheckFileExists = true,
            CheckPathExists = true,
            Multiselect = true
        };

        if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(initialDirectory) && System.IO.Directory.Exists(initialDirectory))
            dialog.InitialDirectory = initialDirectory;

        return dialog.ShowDialog() == true ? dialog.FileNames : Array.Empty<string>();
    }).Task;
}
```

**`SaveFileDialogAsync`** — replace body with:
```csharp
public Task<string?> SaveFileDialogAsync(string title, string filter, string defaultFileName, string? initialDirectory = null)
{
    return Application.Current.Dispatcher.InvokeAsync(() =>
    {
        var dialog = new Microsoft.Win32.SaveFileDialog
        {
            Title = title,
            Filter = filter,
            FileName = defaultFileName,
            CheckPathExists = true
        };

        if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(initialDirectory) && System.IO.Directory.Exists(initialDirectory))
            dialog.InitialDirectory = initialDirectory;

        return dialog.ShowDialog() == true ? dialog.FileName : null;
    }).Task;
}
```

**`OpenFolderDialogAsync`** — replace body with:
```csharp
public Task<string?> OpenFolderDialogAsync(string title, string? initialDirectory = null, bool showNewFolderButton = false)
{
    return Application.Current.Dispatcher.InvokeAsync(() =>
    {
        using var dialog = new Forms.FolderBrowserDialog
        {
            Description = title,
            ShowNewFolderButton = showNewFolderButton
        };

        if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(initialDirectory) && System.IO.Directory.Exists(initialDirectory))
            dialog.SelectedPath = initialDirectory;

        return dialog.ShowDialog() == Forms.DialogResult.OK ? dialog.SelectedPath : null;
    }).Task;
}
```

---

### Step 2 — Fix `VideoGeneratorViewModel.cs`

Replace the existing `ForwardPropertyChanged` method with a version that is aware of which sub-VM sent the event and fires additional aliased property change notifications:

```csharp
private void ForwardPropertyChanged(object? sender, PropertyChangedEventArgs e)
{
    if (e.PropertyName == null) return;

    OnPropertyChanged(e.PropertyName);

    // When a sub-VM's CanGenerateVideo changes, also fire the parent VM's
    // correctly-named alias so XAML bindings like IsEnabled="{Binding CanGenerateMochaVideo}" update.
    if (e.PropertyName == "CanGenerateVideo")
    {
        if (sender == VaceVM)
            OnPropertyChanged(nameof(CanGenerateVACEVideo));
        else if (sender == MochaVM)
            OnPropertyChanged(nameof(CanGenerateMochaVideo));
        else if (sender == LTX2AudioVM)
            OnPropertyChanged(nameof(CanGenerateLTX2AudioVideo));
    }
}
```

